From 085eaf28c26c8bae4e3800e00c51a59da09772f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs: T11 execution order -- resume, measure the reverse
 cost, rule gate B

Gate A passed, the queue resumes, the 156 finished episodes stand and the MPC
stays frozen. The only thing still blocking gate B is the reverse cost: the six
commit times are measured on the sixteen seeds the fixed setpoint fails but not
on the thirty-two it completes, so no constant's net over the 48-seed block can
be computed yet.

Authorises parallel evaluation for outcome measurements. The serial rule exists
to protect timing numbers, and episodes are deterministic: the sandbox's 3-to-5
process runs reproduce the lower window's serial 48-seed run bitwise on the
twelve shared seeds, eleven fields identical with no fuel difference above
0.01 N s. Timing still has to be serial single process and run separately. That
turns 192 episodes from six to twelve hours into one or two.

Gate B is then mechanical from summarize_headroom's CONSTANT vs PER-STATE
table: any fully covered constant matching the baseline's 32/48 stops the round
rather than training it.

Carries both negatives forward explicitly -- the T8 learned-versus-baseline
result and the 2.4x to 5.9x fuel price of the rescues -- and flags that Pure
SAC has no training path on precapture_planning, which is the upper window's
call and does not block anything here.

